From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 00:34:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] phy: samsung-ufs: Let an SoC place the two calibration waits

Both waits are pinned to one point of the sequence and to one side of
the table at that point: the calibration wait runs after the table of
the very first point, the lock wait after the table of the last one.

A calibration whose own work finishes later than the first point has
nowhere to say so, and waiting at the first point would poll for a bit
that has not been set going yet.  A calibration that has to see the lock
before the last table is written, rather than after, has the same
problem in the other direction: the table would be written into a
receiver that has not locked on.

Let the SoC name the point its calibration wait belongs to, and say
whether its lock wait comes before the table or after it.  Both default
to what is done today, so no SoC supported so far changes behaviour.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-ufs.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-ufs.h | 10 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-ufs.c b/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-ufs.c
index 47a7f2916fd..b5c0ba515fe 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-ufs.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-ufs.c
@@ -130,6 +130,16 @@ static int samsung_ufs_phy_calibrate(struct phy *phy)
 	if (!cfg)
 		goto out;
 
+	if (ufs_phy->ufs_phy_state == CFG_POST_PWR_HS &&
+	    ufs_phy->drvdata->wait_for_cdr_before_cfg &&
+	    ufs_phy->drvdata->wait_for_cdr) {
+		for_each_phy_lane(ufs_phy, i) {
+			err = ufs_phy->drvdata->wait_for_cdr(phy, i);
+			if (err)
+				goto out;
+		}
+	}
+
 	for_each_phy_cfg(cfg) {
 		if (!samsung_ufs_phy_cfg_applies(ufs_phy, cfg))
 			continue;
@@ -140,7 +150,7 @@ static int samsung_ufs_phy_calibrate(struct phy *phy)
 	}
 
 	for_each_phy_lane(ufs_phy, i) {
-		if (ufs_phy->ufs_phy_state == CFG_PRE_INIT &&
+		if (ufs_phy->ufs_phy_state == ufs_phy->drvdata->wait_for_cal_state &&
 		    ufs_phy->drvdata->wait_for_cal) {
 			err = ufs_phy->drvdata->wait_for_cal(phy, i);
 			if (err)
@@ -148,6 +158,7 @@ static int samsung_ufs_phy_calibrate(struct phy *phy)
 		}
 
 		if (ufs_phy->ufs_phy_state == CFG_POST_PWR_HS &&
+		    !ufs_phy->drvdata->wait_for_cdr_before_cfg &&
 		    ufs_phy->drvdata->wait_for_cdr) {
 			err = ufs_phy->drvdata->wait_for_cdr(phy, i);
 			if (err)
diff --git a/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-ufs.h b/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-ufs.h
index 3904a63f933..94b28724000 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-ufs.h
+++ b/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-ufs.h
@@ -122,6 +122,16 @@ struct samsung_ufs_phy_drvdata {
 	const char * const *clk_list;
 	int num_clks;
 	u32 cdr_lock_status_offset;
+	/*
+	 * Where in the sequence the two waits below belong.  Left at zero they
+	 * keep to what every SoC described so far needs: the calibration wait
+	 * after the table of the first point, the lock wait after the table of
+	 * the last one.  A calibration that finishes at a later point, or that
+	 * has to see the lock before the last table is written rather than
+	 * after, says so here.
+	 */
+	u8 wait_for_cal_state;
+	bool wait_for_cdr_before_cfg;
 	/* SoC's specific operations */
 	int (*wait_for_cal)(struct phy *phy, u8 lane);
 	int (*wait_for_cdr)(struct phy *phy, u8 lane);
